dex translator: compact locals, a last rescue before the oversize stub

Local slots are numbered in order of first appearance, per (register,
reading). A load/store of slot 0-3 is 1 byte, of 4-255 is 2, of 256+ is 4
(wide). A method with several hundred registers therefore pays the wide form
on most accesses. Translator.COMPACT_LOCALS numbers the slots hottest-first
instead; DexConverter arms it only for a method every other transform failed
to bring under 65535, retranslates with no outlining or splitting, and keeps
the result only if it fits. Every method that already fits is byte-identical.

Measured on Instagram 455 (228,034 classes): exactly one class changes.
    RESCUED X/09IF.A0p(LX/013g;)LX/06Vi;  code_length 68700 -> 61730
    X/0bRx.getValues()[I                   73744 -> 68914  (still stubbed)
A0p is the Litho component that renders a Reel: 805 slots, 492 try ranges and
loops, which the splitter cannot cut. As a stub it made every Reel -- and any
video opened with sound -- draw "Esse reel está indisponível".

Applies to the overlay in src/dex (Translator.java, DexConverter.java).

