+     *
+     * <p>Why it shrinks a method: a load or store of slot 0-3 is 1 byte, of
+     * slot 4-255 is 2 bytes, and of slot 256+ is 4 (the {@code wide} form,
+     * JVMS 6.5). Slots are handed out per (register, reading), so a method
+     * with several hundred registers puts most of them past 255 and pays the
+     * wide form on the majority of its accesses -- including for the registers
+     * it touches most, when those first appear late. Numbering by use count
+     * gives the short forms to the accesses that are executed and emitted
+     * most. Nothing else changes: the same instructions, the same frames (the
